Rem ==================================================================
Rem seedregextest.shoddy — test program for seedregex.shoddy
Rem
Rem Assert-driven, in the seedsimplextest / seedhttpstest pattern: it
Rem prints what it is doing and stops the run at the first assertion
Rem that fails, ending with ALL ASSERTIONS PASSED when it does not.
Rem
Rem WHAT IS GRADED HERE IS THE BRIDGE AND NOT THE ENGINE.
Rem tst/regextest.shoddy grades regex.shoddy — the dialect, the
Rem semantics, and a thousand differential cells against a second
Rem matcher. This file grades the eight lines of glue between that
Rem machine and a keyboard, which is a different and much smaller thing:
Rem does the right cell come back, does a wrong cell refuse instead of
Rem aborting, and does the session survive.
Rem
Rem THE GUARD LIST IS THE TEST LIST. Every refusal the seed can produce
Rem is walked exactly once:
Rem
Rem   * each word given a cell that is not a STRING, which RckKindWhy
Rem     names;
Rem   * each word given a pattern that does not read, which comes back
Rem     as RxRead's own reason and offset.
Rem
Rem AND SURVIVAL IS PROVED BY THE NEXT LINE, never by the refusal. The
Rem Refuses helper below asserts three things at once: the line was
Rem refused, the stack is untouched by it, and a further line evaluated
Rem afterwards answers exactly what it would have answered if the bad
Rem line had never been typed. A refusal that quietly ate a cell would
Rem pass the first of those and fail the third, which is the whole
Rem reason the third is there.
Rem
Rem THE SEED CANNOT ABORT, AND THIS IS NOT AN ACHIEVEMENT OF THE SEED.
Rem regex.shoddy has not one call to Error in it, so there is no
Rem aborting path into the machine for this file to have to avoid. That
Rem is seedhttps's situation and better: its own note is that
Rem https.shoddy "has not one Error in it", which is what made it the
Rem easiest of them all. This machine was written that way from the
Rem start, deliberately, because these words go on a keyboard whose mill
Rem asserts that nothing keyable aborts.
Rem
Rem THE DOCUMENTED LOSS IS ASSERTED AS A LOSS. RXGROUPS flattens an
Rem unset group to "", because a Cell cannot carry the difference. The
Rem assertion below says so in its own text rather than reading as
Rem correct behaviour, so nobody later mistakes it for the contract
Rem regex.shoddy actually keeps.
Rem
Rem Nothing here touches a file, a socket or a window.
Rem
Rem Run: bin\mill run tst\seedregextest.shoddy    (from the repo root)
Rem ==================================================================

Include "../machines/cuttle.shoddy"
Include "../machines/reckoner.shoddy"
Include "../machines/seq.shoddy"
Include "../machines/str.shoddy"
Include "../machines/seeds/seedregex.shoddy"

Rem ---- reading an answer ----------------------------------------------

Def Ran(st As RckState, line As String) As RckState
    Select Case RckEval(st, line)
        Case RckNext(st2, out)
            st2
        Case RckStop(st2, why, out)
            st2
        Case Else
            st

Def Bad(st As RckState, line As String) As Boolean
    Select Case RckEval(st, line)
        Case RckStop(st2, why, out)
            True
        Case Else
            False

Def Why(st As RckState, line As String) As String
    Select Case RckEval(st, line)
        Case RckStop(st2, why, out)
            why
        Case Else
            ""

Def Text(st As RckState) As String
    Join(Map(CutCells(RckStack(st)), Fn(c) => CutShow(c, RckFmt(st))), " | ")

Rem What one line leaves on an empty stack, as a string.
Def Said(line As String) As String
    Text(Ran(RckSeedRegex(RckNew()), line))

Rem Refused, with the reason naming what is wrong; the stack untouched;
Rem and a further line afterwards answering as though nothing happened.
Def Refuses(st As RckState, line As String, why As String) As Boolean
    Bad(st, line) And Instr(Why(st, line), why) > 0 And Text(Ran(st, line)) = Text(st) And Text(Ran(Ran(st, line), "1 1 +")) = Text(Ran(st, "1 1 +"))

Def Qm() As String
    RckQuoteMark()

Def Q(s As String) As String
    Qm() & s & Qm()

Rem A ( s pat -- ) line, which is six of the eight words.
Def Two(subj As String, pat As String, word As String) As String
    Q(subj) & " " & Q(pat) & " " & word

Rem A LIST cell as the reckoner renders one, so an expected answer below
Rem reads as the list it is rather than as a wall of escaped quotes.
Def Lst(xs As List Of String) As String
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        "{ }"
    Else
        "{ " & Join(Map(xs, Q), " ") & " }"

Def Main()
    Let s0 = RckSeedRegex(RckNew())

    Print("--- the eight words are registered, with their metadata ---")
    Assert(RckKnows(s0, "RXTEST") And RckKnows(s0, "RXFIND") And RckKnows(s0, "RXFINDALL") And RckKnows(s0, "RXGROUPS"), "THE FOUR ASKING WORDS ARE IN THE DICTIONARY")
    Assert(RckKnows(s0, "RXREPLACE") And RckKnows(s0, "RXSPLIT") And RckKnows(s0, "RXQUOTE") And RckKnows(s0, "RXWHY"), "AND THE FOUR THAT REWRITE, ESCAPE AND EXPLAIN")
    Rem The seed's own eight, picked out of the dictionary the core has
    Rem already filled, so what follows is about this seed and not about
    Rem what it was folded into.
    Let mine = Filter(RckDict(s0), Fn(e) => WordSeed(e) = "seed-regex")
    Assert(Length(mine) = 8, "EIGHT WORDS, AND NOT A NINTH")
    Assert(IsEmpty(Filter(mine, Fn(e) => WordEffect(e) = "" Or WordDesc(e) = "")), "AND NOT ONE OF THEM IS WITHOUT AN EFFECT LINE AND A DESCRIPTION")
    Assert(All(mine, Fn(e) => Not RckTouches(e)), "EVERY WORD HERE IS PURE — NOTHING IN THIS SEED TOUCHES THE WORLD")
    Assert(All(mine, Fn(e) => StartsWith(WordName(e), "RX")), "AND EVERY ONE IS PREFIXED RX, WHICH IS FREE ACROSS THE WHOLE REGISTERED DICTIONARY")

    Print("--- RXTEST ---")
    Assert(Said(Two("xxabcyy", "abc", "RXTEST")) = "True", "A PATTERN THAT MATCHES ANSWERS TRUE")
    Assert(Said(Two("xxx", "abc", "RXTEST")) = "False", "AND ONE THAT DOES NOT ANSWERS FALSE")
    Assert(Said(Two("2026-08-08", "^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$", "RXTEST")) = "True", "A STATED RULE, READ AS THE RULE IT IS")
    Assert(Said(Two("2026-8-8", "^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$", "RXTEST")) = "False", "AND THE SAME RULE SAYING NO")

    Print("--- RXFIND pushes two cells, always ---")
    Rem Text renders the stack TOP FIRST, so a start of 1 and a length
    Rem of 3 reads "3 | 1". The word pushes the start and then the
    Rem length, which is the order the effect line states.
    Assert(Said(Two("xxabcyy", "abc", "RXFIND")) = "3 | 3", "THE 1-BASED START AND THE LENGTH")
    Assert(Said(Two("xxx", "abc", "RXFIND")) = "0 | 0", "AND 0 0 WHERE THERE IS NO MATCH — TWO CELLS EITHER WAY, WHICH IS WHAT UNDO'S ACCOUNTING NEEDS")
    Assert(Said(Two("aaa", "a*", "RXFIND")) = "3 | 1", "AN EMPTY-CAPABLE PATTERN STILL ANSWERS ITS LONGEST LEFTMOST MATCH")

    Print("--- RXFINDALL ---")
    Assert(Said(Two("a1b22c333", "\\d+", "RXFINDALL")) = Lst({ "1", "22", "333" }), "EVERY NON-OVERLAPPING MATCH, IN ORDER")
    Assert(Said(Two("xxx", "\\d", "RXFINDALL")) = Lst({ }), "AND AN EMPTY LIST WHERE THERE ARE NONE")
    Assert(Said(Two("baa", "a*", "RXFINDALL")) = Lst({ "", "aa", "" }), "AND THE EMPTY-MATCH RULE GIVES THREE OVER baa, TWO OF THEM EMPTY")

    Print("--- RXGROUPS, and the distinction the bridge cannot carry ---")
    Assert(Said(Two("me@here", "(\\w+)@(\\w+)", "RXGROUPS")) = Lst({ "me@here", "me", "here" }), "THE WHOLE MATCH FIRST, THEN ONE ITEM PER GROUP")
    Assert(Said(Two("xxx", "(a)", "RXGROUPS")) = Lst({ }), "AND AN EMPTY LIST WHERE THERE IS NO MATCH")
    Rem THE DOCUMENTED LOSS. RxGroup answers None() for group 1 here and
    Rem Some("b") for group 2; a Cell cannot carry None, so both arrive
    Rem as STRINGs and the unset one is "".
    Assert(Said(Two("b", "(a)|(b)", "RXGROUPS")) = Lst({ "b", "", "b" }), "AN UNSET GROUP ARRIVES AS AN EMPTY STRING — THE DISTINCTION RxGroup KEEPS DOES NOT SURVIVE THE Cell TYPE, AND THAT IS THE DOCUMENTED LOSS AND NOT THE CONTRACT")

    Print("--- RXREPLACE ---")
    Assert(Said(Q("banana") & " " & Q("[aeiou]") & " " & Q("-") & " RXREPLACE") = Q("b-n-n-"), "EVERY MATCH REPLACED")
    Assert(Said(Q("me@here") & " " & Q("(\\w+)@(\\w+)") & " " & Q("$2/$1") & " RXREPLACE") = Q("here/me"), "AND A TEMPLATE READS ITS GROUPS")
    Assert(Said(Q("ab") & " " & Q("b") & " " & Q("$$") & " RXREPLACE") = Q("a$"), "AND $$ IS A LITERAL DOLLAR")

    Print("--- RXSPLIT ---")
    Assert(Said(Two("a, b,c", ",\\s*", "RXSPLIT")) = Lst({ "a", "b", "c" }), "CUT APART ON A PATTERN, WHICH IS THREE PASSES WITH A LITERAL SEPARATOR")
    Assert(Said(Two("abc", "abc", "RXSPLIT")) = Lst({ "", "" }), "A PATTERN MATCHING THE WHOLE SUBJECT GIVES TWO EMPTY PIECES")
    Assert(Said(Two("a,b", "(,)", "RXSPLIT")) = Lst({ "a", "b" }), "AND A CAPTURING GROUP DOES NOT PUT ITS SEPARATOR INTO THE RESULT")

    Print("--- RXQUOTE ---")
    Assert(Said(Q("a.b*c") & " RXQUOTE") = Q("a\\.b\\*c"), "THE METACHARACTERS ESCAPED")
    Assert(Said(Q("a.b*c") & " RXQUOTE " & Q("a.b*c") & " SWAP RXTEST") = "True", "AND WHAT COMES BACK MATCHES THE ORIGINAL")
    Assert(Said(Q("a.b*c") & " RXQUOTE " & Q("axbbbc") & " SWAP RXTEST") = "False", "AND NOT WHAT THE ORIGINAL LOOKED LIKE")

    Print("--- RXWHY ---")
    Assert(Said(Q("a(b)c") & " RXWHY") = Q(""), "A PATTERN THAT READS HAS NOTHING WRONG WITH IT")
    Assert(Instr(Said(Q("(a") & " RXWHY"), "UNMATCHED (") > 0, "AND ONE THAT DOES NOT SAYS WHY")
    Assert(Instr(Said(Q("(a") & " RXWHY"), "(at 1)") > 0, "AND WHERE — WHICH IS WHAT TURNS A MISTYPED PATTERN INTO A FIXED ONE")
    Assert(Instr(Said(Q("(a)\\1") & " RXWHY"), "BACKREFERENCES") > 0, "AND A REFUSED CONSTRUCT IS NAMED RATHER THAN CALLED UNEXPECTED")

    Print("--- every word refuses a cell that is not a STRING ---")
    Rem One line per word, and the helper proves the mill survived each.
    Let s1 = Ran(s0, "1 2")
    Assert(Refuses(s1, "3 4 RXTEST", "RXTEST needs"), "RXTEST")
    Assert(Refuses(s1, "3 4 RXFIND", "RXFIND needs"), "RXFIND")
    Assert(Refuses(s1, "3 4 RXFINDALL", "RXFINDALL needs"), "RXFINDALL")
    Assert(Refuses(s1, "3 4 RXGROUPS", "RXGROUPS needs"), "RXGROUPS")
    Assert(Refuses(s1, "3 4 5 RXREPLACE", "RXREPLACE needs"), "RXREPLACE")
    Assert(Refuses(s1, "3 4 RXSPLIT", "RXSPLIT needs"), "RXSPLIT")
    Assert(Refuses(s1, "3 RXQUOTE", "RXQUOTE needs"), "RXQUOTE")
    Assert(Refuses(s1, "3 RXWHY", "RXWHY needs"), "RXWHY")
    Rem And with only the SECOND argument wrong, which is a different
    Rem arm of the same guard.
    Assert(Refuses(s1, Q("abc") & " 4 RXTEST", "RXTEST needs"), "AND WHEN IT IS THE PATTERN THAT IS NOT A STRING")
    Assert(Refuses(s1, Q("abc") & " " & Q("a") & " 5 RXREPLACE", "RXREPLACE needs"), "AND WHEN IT IS THE REPLACEMENT")

    Print("--- every word refuses a pattern that does not read ---")
    Assert(Refuses(s1, Two("abc", "(", "RXTEST"), "UNMATCHED ("), "RXTEST")
    Assert(Refuses(s1, Two("abc", "(", "RXFIND"), "UNMATCHED ("), "RXFIND")
    Assert(Refuses(s1, Two("abc", "[", "RXFINDALL"), "UNTERMINATED ["), "RXFINDALL")
    Assert(Refuses(s1, Two("abc", "*", "RXGROUPS"), "NOTHING TO REPEAT"), "RXGROUPS")
    Assert(Refuses(s1, Q("abc") & " " & Q("(a") & " " & Q("x") & " RXREPLACE", "UNMATCHED ("), "RXREPLACE")
    Assert(Refuses(s1, Two("abc", "a{9999}", "RXSPLIT"), "TOO MANY REPETITIONS"), "RXSPLIT")
    Rem RXQUOTE takes no pattern, and RXWHY answers rather than refuses —
    Rem which is the point of RXWHY existing at all.
    Assert(Not Bad(s1, Q("(a") & " RXWHY"), "RXWHY DOES NOT REFUSE A BAD PATTERN — IT REPORTS ONE, WHICH IS WHY IT IS THERE")
    Assert(Refuses(s1, Two("abc", "(?=a)", "RXTEST"), "LOOKAHEAD"), "AND A CONSTRUCT PAST THE CEILING IS REFUSED BY NAME AT THE KEYBOARD TOO")
    Assert(Refuses(s1, Two("abc", "a{9999}", "RXTEST"), "2000"), "AND THE SIZE CAP NAMES ITS NUMBER AT THE KEYBOARD TOO")

    Print("--- and the mill is still answering ---")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s1, "3 4 +")) = "7 | 2 | 1", "3 4 + STILL ANSWERS 7, AFTER EVERY REFUSAL ABOVE")

    Print("")
    Print("ALL ASSERTIONS PASSED")
